(VAR-63: file paths are claimed to be data that stays double-quoted. `see`
 takes a single-quoted path too, and really includes the file — the fixture
 prints. So the "stay double-quoted" rule is not enforced here, and a single
 quoted token means an identifier in most positions and a data string in
 `see` position, which is the context-sensitivity LANGUAGE.md:659-660 says
 does not exist. See Discrepancy 5. `./` in a `see` resolves against the
 directory of the file that writes it, so this probe runs from anywhere.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox VAR-63.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   helper included
   the single-quoted path was accepted
)
see './fixtures/helper.vox'.
Print "the single-quoted path was accepted".
